Feature: MOON-544 Select Multiple Tests and Bundles — All Possible Integration Tests

  Background:
    Given I navigate to the Moonshot benchmark workflow from the landing page
    And I am on the "Select Test Bundles" page

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------
  # AC1: User can select multiple bundles in bulk
  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------

  Scenario: Configure button is disabled when no bundles are selected
    Given no bundle toggle is selected
    Then the "Configure and Run Benchmark Tests" button is disabled
    And the selected tests sidebar shows no selected bundles

  Scenario: Selecting multiple bundles enables bulk progression
    Given at least two bundle cards are visible
    When I select bundle A
    And I select bundle B
    Then bundle A and bundle B show selected state
    And the "Configure and Run Benchmark Tests" button is enabled
    And both bundles appear in the selected tests sidebar

  Scenario: Deselecting one bundle keeps other selected bundles intact
    Given bundle A and bundle B are selected
    When I deselect bundle A
    Then bundle B remains selected
    And only bundle B remains in the selected tests sidebar
    And the "Configure and Run Benchmark Tests" button remains enabled

  Scenario: Deselecting all selected bundles disables bulk progression
    Given one or more bundles are selected
    When I deselect every selected bundle
    Then the "Configure and Run Benchmark Tests" button is disabled
    And the selected tests sidebar is empty

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------
  # AC2: User can manage multiple tests across selected bundles
  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------

  Scenario: Selecting a bundle auto-selects all tests in that bundle
    Given bundle A has one or more tests
    When I select bundle A from the bundle card toggle
    Then all tests under bundle A are selected in the sidebar
    And bundle A selected count shows full selection (selected == total)

  Scenario: User can partially deselect tests in a selected bundle
    Given bundle A is selected with all tests selected
    When I uncheck one test under bundle A in the sidebar
    Then the bundle A selected count decreases by one
    And bundle A remains present in the selected bundles list
    And I can continue managing selections for other bundles

  Scenario: User can manage tests independently across multiple bundles
    Given bundle A and bundle B are selected
    When I uncheck one test in bundle A
    And I keep all tests selected in bundle B
    Then bundle A shows partial selected count
    And bundle B shows full selected count
    And both bundles remain available for bulk run setup

  Scenario: Bundle details sheet supports per-test bulk curation before adding
    Given I open "Learn more" for bundle A
    When I toggle test selections inside the bundle details sheet
    Then the sheet action button text reflects selected quantity (for example "Add 1 test" or "Add N tests")
    And the sheet action button is disabled when zero tests are selected
    And the sheet action button is enabled when at least one test is selected

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------
  # AC3: Bulk run request reflects multi-bundle and multi-test selections
  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------

  Scenario: Run request with full selections across multiple bundles omits tests_by_bundle
    Given bundle A and bundle B are selected
    And all tests in bundle A and bundle B are selected
    And I complete required model or application configuration
    When I start the benchmark run
    Then the POST "/api/start-benchmark-run" request contains both bundle ids in "bundle_names"
    And the request does not include "tests_by_bundle"

  Scenario: Run request with partial selection includes tests_by_bundle only for partial bundles
    Given bundle A and bundle B are selected
    And bundle A has partial test selection
    And bundle B has full test selection
    And I complete required model or application configuration
    When I start the benchmark run
    Then the POST "/api/start-benchmark-run" request contains bundle A and bundle B in "bundle_names"
    And the request includes "tests_by_bundle" for bundle A only
    And the tests list for bundle A contains benchmark_test_id values of selected tests
    And "tests_by_bundle" does not include bundle B

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------
  # AC4: Bulk selection state is preserved while navigating within workflow
  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------

  Scenario: Returning from model selection preserves selected bundles and tests
    Given I selected multiple bundles and modified per-test selections
    When I proceed to model selection
    And I click "Back to Bundle Selection"
    Then previously selected bundles remain selected
    And previously selected per-test selections remain intact
    And selected counts in the sidebar match the prior state

  # NOT integration-testable: "more efficiently in bulk" is a productivity outcome
  # and cannot be directly asserted with deterministic UI/API integration checks.
